stroke motif, how the head lands on the sam, how the hook and the riff share accents and
attacks, whether it is unmistakably this raga, and whether it answers the request.
Then return YOUR seed (`seed`): revise it where the rival or the numbers persuaded you — take
a principle, never the rival's notes — and return it unchanged where yours is already the
stronger idea (`changed`: false). Do not merge the two ideas: your seed stays your own. Every
hard rule above still applies to it.

